schema_version	scope	severity	focus_area	location	what	scenario_or_breakage	suggested_fix
1	in_scope	important	risk-integration	skills/design/SKILL.md:103-158; plan.txt:76-82	Planned log PR runs on the active design or implement branch	In nested /design, branch_info_supplied=true means /implement's active feature branch is reused; the planned publish step commits logs, opens or reuses a PR, admin-merges it, and deletes the branch before /implement has run. In standalone /design from main, CURRENT_BRANCH can also be stale after Step 1 creates a new branch.	Do not publish from CURRENT_BRANCH. Create a dedicated larch-log branch per design run from the default branch, validate the checked-out branch before push, and skip/route differently when SESSION_ENV_PATH is non-empty.
1	in_scope	important	correctness	scripts/create-pr.sh:117-157; plan.txt:36-38; plan.txt:122	create-pr existing-PR fast path can admin-merge unrelated work	create-pr.sh returns PR_STATUS=existing for any open PR on the current branch, and the plan explicitly proceeds to gh pr merge on that PR number. A user running /design on a branch that already has an implementation PR would merge all branch contents with --admin, not just design logs.	Require a dedicated log branch and reject PR_STATUS=existing unless the head branch, title, and diff are exactly the expected design-log PR; preferably avoid create-pr.sh's existing-PR path for this workflow.
1	in_scope	important	security	docs/run-logs.md:60-67; scripts/larch-log.sh:101-115; plan.txt:29-31	Raw sidecar files would be committed without existing sidecar trimming	The plan copies all depth-1 DESIGN_TMPDIR files with only tmpdir and secret redaction, including .meta and JSON sidecars. Existing committed run-log policy strips CMD_JSON from .meta and removes top-level .result from output JSON because those fields can contain full prompts, commands, or raw model output not intended for logs.	Use an explicit allowlist plus the existing larch-log sidecar trimmers, or factor stage_round_artifact-style handling into a shared helper and fail closed on trim failure.
1	in_scope	important	architecture	plan.txt:67-82; skills/design/SKILL.md:105-158	The Step 5 snippet calls plugin scripts through PATH or relative cwd	tracking-issue-write.sh is not called with ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts, and scripts/design-log-publish.sh is relative to the operator cwd. In plugin-consumer mode this can fail with command-not-found or execute a consumer repo script with the same path.	Use "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh" and "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/design-log-publish.sh"; inside the new script, resolve sibling helpers from its own SCRIPT_DIR.
1	in_scope	latent	code-quality	plan.txt:72-84	Warning paths use print inside a bash snippet	The planned Step 5 code block uses print for warnings. Bash 3.2 does not provide print, so the warning path can produce command not found and, depending on surrounding set -e behavior, mask the original best-effort failure.	Use printf '%s\n' '...' in bash snippets, or keep Print directives outside fenced shell code.

1. [risk-integration] `skills/design/SKILL.md:103-158`, `plan.txt:76-82`: The planned log publishing runs against the active branch. In nested `/design`, that is `/implement`'s branch; in standalone `/design`, `CURRENT_BRANCH` may be stale after Step 1 branch creation. Use a dedicated per-run log branch and skip or defer this path in nested mode.

2. [correctness] `scripts/create-pr.sh:117-157`, `plan.txt:36-38`, `plan.txt:122`: Treating an existing PR as safe is dangerous here. The plan would admin-merge any open PR on the branch, possibly real implementation work. Reject existing PRs unless they are proven to be the expected log-only PR.

3. [security] `docs/run-logs.md:60-67`, `scripts/larch-log.sh:101-115`, `plan.txt:29-31`: The plan bypasses existing `.meta` and JSON sidecar trimming and commits all `DESIGN_TMPDIR` files after only broad redaction. Reuse the existing trimming semantics or add a design-specific allowlist and fail closed.

4. [architecture] `plan.txt:67-82`, `skills/design/SKILL.md:105-158`: The new Step 5 calls are not rooted at `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`. In consumer repos this can fail or hit the wrong script. Root every plugin helper call at `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts`.

5. [code-quality] `plan.txt:72-84`: `print` is inside a bash snippet, but Bash 3.2 has no `print` builtin. Use `printf '%s\n' ...` for warning output.
